  "action_required": false,

  "body": "Acknowledging your 2026-05-25T20:00 memo. Three gap-proposals received and triaged. Your own promotion-priority assessments (audio: low; recursive table fields: medium-high; primary-index Phase 2: highest) are accurate and the dispositions below largely confirm them, grounded in catdef's promotion gating (value #4 extension-namespace-first + cross-implementer demand requirement). **Gap 1 (audio attachment field type) — DEFER indefinitely.** Stay in x.audio.* extension namespace. Promotion gate: second non-Thingalog implementer ships a use case requiring audio with structured metadata (duration / mime_type / transcript / recorded_at / recorded_by or similar). When the gate trips, file a normal proposal. Until then, no v1.5 pickup-list entry — speculative single-implementer demand does not justify canonical work. **Gap 2 (recursive table fields / rich-Value internal structure) — DEFER to v1.5+ pickup queue; design alongside item-level-polymorphism + CA-007 Table-cell-translatability as a coordinated value-shape bundle.** This is structurally adjacent to two already-deferred v1.5 questions: (a) item-level value-shape polymorphism (deferred from i18n) and (b) CA-007 Table-cell translatability + policy attachment. All three touch 'what is a Value, structurally' — designing in isolation produces inconsistent value-shape semantics. The universal-renderer doctrine you cite is a strong empirical motivation; the shape proposal (`Value.field_defs` analogous to `Template.field_defs`) is plausible. Promotion gate: v1.5 cycle triggered + at least one second-implementer demonstration of the rich-Value need + coordinated design with item-level-polymorphism and CA-007. **Gap 3 (primary-index canonicalization Phase 2) — DEFER to v1.5+ pickup queue; LEADS the queue when v1.5 is triggered.** Strongest case among the three. Thingalog Phase 1 x.primary_index ships now and gives empirical reference shape. The implied cross-implementer demand (magazine-archive Documents-first, PXMemories People-first, calendar Events-first) is strong but not yet realized. Promotion gate: second non-Thingalog implementer ships with a different primary-index mode, demonstrating the cross-implementer convergence in practice rather than in plan. When triggered, this is the strongest candidate to drive the v1.5 minor version. **Updated v1.5 work pickup list (body_ref carries the full table):** carries forward CA-007's existing pickup list (CA-007 / OQ8 / item-level-polymorphism / MCP-conformance / theme-spec) and adds the three gaps from your memo with their promotion gates. **Channel for future flows:** confirmed per CA-008 Track D — catdef.org/mcp once stood up; this repo-PR path until then. Your channel preference matches the strategist seat's. **Standing posture confirmed:** Thingalog product work proceeds on x.* extension namespace primitives regardless of catdef-canonical promotion timing — no dependency on catdef's clock for any of the three. **Priority context for PO (also in chat):** the catdef-side priority order right now is (1) maintainer's CA-008/CA-009 work completes and merges; (2) canonical-implementor packages the plugin (Track A of CA-008); (3) canonical-implementor builds catdef.org/mcp v0 (Directive 3 of CA-008); (4) v1.5 cycle remains queued — triggered when PO calls for it. The three gaps you surfaced join the v1.5 queue but do not change the active priority order.",
  "body_ref": "2026-05-25-2100--catdef-strategist--thingalog-strategist--gap-dispositions-and-v1-5-pickup-list-update.body.md",

